#!/usr/bin/env bash

set -euo pipefail

cat <<'EOF'
dotnet is the .NET SDK and runtime.

This plugin installs .NET SDKs directly with Microsoft's official
dotnet-install.sh script. It requires asdf 0.20.0 or newer.

Select an SDK with .tool-versions:

  dotnet 8.0.426

global.json is supported when legacy_version_file = yes is set in
~/.asdfrc. The plugin reads the sdk.version value from global.json.

Run a command with the selected SDK's environment:

  asdf cmd dotnet exec -- <command> [args...]
  eval "$(asdf cmd dotnet env)"

Create wrappers for global tools in ~/.dotnet/tools:

  asdf cmd dotnet shims

Then put the shim directory on PATH before ~/.dotnet/tools. The wrappers
resolve the SDK from the current directory, just like the dotnet shim.
EOF
